# These files are alphabetically-sorted, block-based lists (role-specific
# markers). Upstream and our custom roles (roles/custom/*) both insert new
# blocks near each other, which git's default merge frequently flags as a
# conflict even though both insertions are independent additions.
#
# `merge=union` makes git keep both sides' lines automatically instead of
# raising a conflict. Worst case: a duplicated role-specific block, which is
# harmless here (each block is gated by its own `*_enabled` conditional) and
# easy to spot - see `just --justfile justfile.upstream update`'s
# post-merge duplicate check.
templates/setup.yml merge=union
templates/group_vars_mash_servers merge=union
